      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Managed conservation is a fundamentally flawed, anthropocentric approach that treats nature as a resource to be managed for human benefit, which is inherently unsustainable. This outdated model imposes human will onto complex ecological systems, often leading to artificial interventions that mask underlying problems. Rewilding, conversely, embraces ecological dynamism by allowing natural processes to take the lead, restoring self-regulating ecosystems that are truly resilient. We must shift our focus from controlling nature to facilitating its inherent capacity for recovery.",
      "source": "target",
